(:frozenPaths :v 1
  :doc "Suites switched off while only the LLVM native target matters (principal decision 2026-10-11); the code they cover stays, ported later via the AST to TypeScript, WebAssembly, shell, HTML/CSS/JS or C. Read by asl-gates/suiteRunner discover and named-directory selection, asl-cli sweep (bare asl test and --changed), asl/tools/testImpact and tools/fleet/compare touchedSuites. :kind package freezes every suite under :path; :kind suite freezes exactly that file. A named directory skips frozen suites and reports their count; naming a frozen suite explicitly as a file still runs it. This ledger only grows by principal decision; it does not shrink knownRed. Freezing stays per-suite, not per-package, wherever a package also carries live infra: asl-target-sh/src/distrib.asl renders scripts/install.sh and asl/dist/install.sh (install.sh --render-rules/--check-rules depend on it) and asl-target-sh/src/rules.asl is its renderer; distribTest.asl and installParityTest.asl cover that live infra and stay frozen separately for an unrelated HL-E-MISC host-migration reason, while the rest of asl-target-sh (the shell/PowerShell compile-target backend: astTest.asl emitPs1Test.asl emitShTest.asl lowerTest.asl) and the swift/ts/sh acceptance suites unfroze on 2026-10-15 (TGTTRIM, principal decision): their unit tests pass natively, but asl-target-sh and asl-target-swift still only emit stub/raw-text function bodies (see capabilities.asn shTarget/swiftTarget :lies), so a passing suite here means the test is green, not that the target works; asl-codegen/c99Emit and c99Mangle feed asl-compiler/src/compiler.asl's compilePackageToC99!, exercised directly by asl-compiler/tests/c99TargetTest.asl and entryDirResolutionTest.asl (tools/compileFile.asl, a dead CLI wrapper around the same call with 0 importers, was removed in STRUCTB), so c99AbiBridgeTest.asl and c99TargetTest.asl stay live too (PRUNE-SURVEY, 2026-10-11)."
