  (:frozen :path "tests/host/parTest.asl" :kind suite :reason "HL-DELETE (asl/host/src deleted, stage-0 host retired): 8 of 10 test functions are trivially fixed (resolveHost! now returns the literal \"bin/asl\"; confirmed each of testWorkerTrap!/testLastWorkerTrap!/testSlotsArg!/testChildPrint!/testSequentialFallback!'s ERR_WORKER_TRAP/ERR_ARG/stdout/fallback behavior reproduces identically under bin/asl eval by hand), but two do not: testGcStress! hits the nativeCli GC_STRESS architecture issue (ASL_GC_STRESS=1 in the parent env makes bin/asl's own native-CLI self-check pathologically slow; confirmed by hand, a reduced repro of this exact call hangs past a 30s perl alarm, killed cleanly with no orphans this time); testMalformedFrames! compiles and runs tests/host/parallelDeserTest.c directly against -Iasl/host/src headers and asl/host/out/libaslhost.a, a standalone C unit test of the host's wire-frame deserializer with no ASL-level equivalent, and both the .c file and the headers/library it needs were deleted along with the stage-0 host in this same unit; freezing the whole suite (frozen.asn has no per-function grain) rather than deleting either function: code and assertions, including both of these, stay fully untouched; unfreezes once nativeCli's GC_STRESS self-check leak is fixed and once the deserializer gets a native fixture or its C unit test is deliberately retired by name" :since "2026-10-13" :by HLDELETE)
