  (:frozen :path "tests/acceptance/r1Host/gcGrowthTest.asl" :kind suite :reason "HL-E-ACC native port: host swapped to ./bin/asl (test/eval verbs are native), but the suite's statOf helper assumes exactly one (:gcStats ...) block per ASL_GC_STATS=1 invocation (its own stringSplit-by-marker check requires listLength=2, else returns -1); confirmed by hand that a single './bin/asl test FILE' or './bin/asl eval EXPR' invocation under ASL_GC_STATS=1 can print TWO distinct (:gcStats ...)/(:gcPhases ...) block pairs with very different magnitudes (seen: a trivial no-op test printed a tiny first block then an unrelated ~170MB-allocation second block; a real 400k-element churn workload printed a ~16MB first block then an unrelated ~236KB second block) - the self-hosted native test/eval pipeline's own internal compile/cache/self-check machinery inherits ASL_GC_STATS and emits its own instrumented block, nondeterministically before or after the workload's depending on cache warmth; statOf's ':bytesLive'/':collections' extraction returns -1 whenever this happens, which it does for 'defaultRes' in a clean run, failing 'the live list keeps more than 15 MB across the churn' after 4 asserts; fixing this reliably needs either isolating the workload's own gcStats block by position (unstable across cache states, confirmed) or a native flag to suppress self-check instrumentation's own stats, neither a trivial swap; code and assertions stay untouched" :since "2026-10-15" :by HLEACC)
