  (:frozen :path "asl/packages/asl-gates/tests/runnerMainTest.asl" :kind suite :reason "HL-FIX3: testRunVerdictParity! (and every later test in this suite's shared-scratch chain: testSingleSnapshotParity!, testTimeoutKillsGroup!, testGateTestsTolerance!) run runnerMain.asl against an isolated 'git clone -q --local' scratch copy of the repo (makeClone!) with injected fixture suites and an edited .asl/mem/knownRed.asn, expecting runAsl! (bin/asl run <root>/asl/packages/asl-gates/src/runnerMain.asl run --suite <relative path>, cwd=clone) to resolve --suite paths and the knownRed ledger against the clone; it never does, hitting both documented native gaps at once: NATIVE-CHDIR (bin/asl always anchors ASL_CLI_ROOT to its own install location, not the caller's cwd) and OUT-OF-ROOT (a path outside that fixed root is refused or, if given directly, silently NATIVE-BYPASS-staged into the real root's own .asl/cache/nativeTest/outside/ instead of being read from the clone); confirmed by hand reproducing outside the test harness, from a throwaway clone+fixture identical to makeClone!'s: 'bin/asl run <realRoot>/.../runnerMain.asl run --suite asl/packages/asl-gates/tests/fixtures/runner/zzProbeTest.asl' (cwd=clone, file written only in the clone) reports '(:check :id suite :status :failed :err ERR_NEW_RED_SUITE :suite \"asl/packages/asl-gates/tests/fixtures/runner/zzProbeTest.asl\" :ev \"ERR_LOAD ... ERR_IO cannot open file\")' plus the REAL root's own current knownRed.asn staleness noise (4 stale asl/web/tests/* entries), not the clone's injected fixtures or edited ledger at all; setting ASL_CLI_ROOT=<clone> in the child env (available at the test level, asl-cli/src/system.asl's own override point) has no effect on this fixed anchoring either; the suite's actual run reproduces exactly: 'FAIL asl/packages/asl-gates/tests/runnerMainTest.asl: ERR_ASSERT: assertion failed: one held, one passing, receipt failed (after 94 asserts)' with the printed receipt showing driftRedTest.asl/heldRedTest.asl both ERR_IO and 4 unrelated asl/web/tests/* ERR_STALE_KNOWN_RED entries, never the clone's own siteClaimsTest/missingTest checks; fixing it means lifting the native CLI's fixed-root anchoring for an isolated clone-and-run harness, a nativeCli.asl/native.asl policy change outside this unit's :owns (same class as HLEMISC's providersTest.asl/nativeMathTest.asl/distribTest.asl freezes); code and assertions stay untouched; unfreezes once bin/asl run can operate against a workspace root other than its own fixed install location, or this suite's harness is rewritten to stay in-root" :since "2026-10-15" :by HLFIX3)
